    summary_60s: 'Atomic Structure and Quantum Theory The understanding of atomic structure has evolved significantly through centuries of scientific investigation. Early theories laid the groundwork for modern quantum mechanics, which now governs our comprehension of matter at the subatomic level',
    key_formulas: '• Number of Moles: n = Mass (g) / Molar Mass (g/mol) = N / N_A [N_A = 6.02 × 10²³]\n• Moles of Gas at s.t.p.: n = Volume (dm³) / 22.4 dm³\n• Percentage Composition = (Mass of element in 1 mole / Molar Mass) × 100%\n• Empirical Formula: Lowest whole-number ratio of atoms',
