    summary_60s: 'Radioactivity: history, types of radiations, radioactive disintegration, nuclear equations, half-life, radioactive carbon, detectors and applications. RADIOACTIVITY Nuclear Reactions and Radioactive Emissions Unlike ordinary chemical reactions, which involve the rearrangement of ',
    key_formulas: '• pH Definition: pH = -log₁₀[H⁺] | pOH = -log₁₀[OH⁻]\n• Water Dissociation: pH + pOH = 14 (at 25°C)\n• Titration Formula: (C_A · V_A) / (C_B · V_B) = n_A / n_B\n• Concentration in g/dm³ = Molarity (mol/dm³) × Molar Mass (g/mol)',
