    summary_60s: 'Atomic theory evolved through several scientific models. Early atomic models could not fully explain experimental observations such as atomic spectra, electron behavior, and chemical bonding. Important scientists contributed to the modern quantum model. Scientist Contribution Nie',
    key_formulas: '• Number of Moles: n = Mass (g) / Molar Mass (g/mol) = N / N_A [N_A = 6.02 × 10²³]\n• Moles of Gas at s.t.p.: n = Volume (dm³) / 22.4 dm³\n• Percentage Composition = (Mass of element in 1 mole / Molar Mass) × 100%\n• Empirical Formula: Lowest whole-number ratio of atoms',
