    id: 1435,
    subject: 'Chemistry',
    exam_type: 'JAMB • WAEC • NECO Standard',
    class_level: 'SS1-SS3 Comprehensive',
    topic: 'ELECTROCHEMISTRY',
    subtopic: 'Electrolysis',
    summary_60s: 'Electrolysis is the splitting of a substance (called an electrolyte) into its component ions by passage of Direct Current through a solution of the compound or through the molten compound. It\'s a redox reaction where electrical energy is converted to chemical energy, causing deco',
    key_formulas: '• Faraday\'s 1st Law: m = ZIt = (M · I · t) / (n · F) [F = 96,500 C/mol]\n• Faraday\'s 2nd Law: m₁/E₁ = m₂/E₂ where E = Molar Mass / Valency\n• Cell Potential: E°cell = E°cathode - E°anode\n• Oxidation: Loss of electrons (at ANODE)\n• Reduction: Gain of electrons (at CATHODE)',
