    summary_60s: 'The earliest evidence of soap dates back to 2800 B.C. , where historians believe it was used by the ancient Babylonians. Soap-making is also mentioned in ancient Roman documents as early as 70 A.D. Detergents emerged around 1916 during World War I, when shortages of soap ingredie',
    key_formulas: '• Alkanes (Saturated): C_n H_(2n+2) [Substitution reactions]\n• Alkenes (Unsaturated C=C): C_n H_2n [Addition reactions]\n• Alkynes (Unsaturated C≡C): C_n H_(2n-2)\n• Alkanols (Alcohols): C_n H_(2n+1)OH\n• Alkanoic Acids: C_n H_(2n+1)COOH',
